<h3 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Q9z1" id=sign-certificate-against-cel-role>Sign certificate against CEL role<a href=#sign-certificate-against-cel-role class=hash-link aria-label="Direct link to Sign certificate against CEL role" title="Direct link to Sign certificate against CEL role" translate=no>​</a></h3>
<p>This endpoint signs a new certificate based upon the provided CSR and the
supplied parameters, subject to the restrictions contained in the role named in
the endpoint. The issuing CA certificate and the full CA chain is returned as
well, so that only the root CA need be in a client's trust store.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th style=text-align:left>Method<th style=text-align:left>Path<th style=text-align:left>Issuer<tbody><tr><td style=text-align:left><code>POST</code><td style=text-align:left><code>/pki/cel/sign/:name</code><td style=text-align:left>Role selected</table>
<h4 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Q9z1" id=parameters-17>Parameters<a href=#parameters-17 class=hash-link aria-label="Direct link to Parameters" title="Direct link to Parameters" translate=no>​</a></h4>
<ul>
<li class="">
<p><code>name</code> <code>(string: &lt;required>)</code> - Specifies the name of the role to create the
certificate against. This is part of the request URL.</p>
</li>
<li class="">
<p><code>csr</code> <code>(string: &lt;required>)</code> - Specifies the PEM-encoded CSR.</p>
</li>
<li class="">
<p>Any arbitrary field can be provided and will be used if recognized in the CEL
program.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<div class="theme-admonition theme-admonition-info admonition_wBnh alert alert--info"><div class=admonitionHeading_kByF><span class=admonitionIcon_jbvL><svg viewBox="0 0 14 16"><path fill-rule=evenodd d="M7 2.3c3.14 0 5.7 2.56 5.7 5.7s-2.56 5.7-5.7 5.7A5.71 5.71 0 0 1 1.3 8c0-3.14 2.56-5.7 5.7-5.7zM7 1C3.14 1 0 4.14 0 8s3.14 7 7 7 7-3.14 7-7-3.14-7-7-7zm1 3H6v5h2V4zm0 6H6v2h2v-2z"/></svg></span>info</div><div class=admonitionContent_FvSw><p><strong>Note</strong> Every key/value pair in the request body is forwarded to the CEL
<strong>request</strong> object. A CEL program may decide which of these parameters to
honour, ignore, or override.</div></div>
